# Dev Notes 19 — Runtime Layout Folder Structure v1

This note records the behavior-preserving physical layout migration after the public entrypoint rename to `runtime.mjs`.

## Purpose

Move parent-runtime internal modules into a `runtime/` folder with subfolders while preserving public runtime behavior and path-sensitive worker/model boundaries.

This change is layout-only. It does not redesign request scheduling, worker execution, lifecycle behavior, prompt/output semantics, config override behavior, retry/profile planning, shutdown/drain semantics, model identity/path resolution, or worker protocol messages.

## Public entrypoint and stable root files

`runtime.mjs` remains the canonical public runtime entrypoint at the repo root.

During the first two layout units, these path-sensitive files were intentionally left at the repo root while parent runtime internals moved first:

```text
config.mjs
configOverride.mjs
contextRetryProfiles.mjs
hardwareProbe.mjs
retryProfiles.mjs
workerBridge.mjs
llama_worker/llama.mjs
```

`docs/dev-notes.20` records the follow-up config/profile helper layout unit, which moved the config/profile helpers into `runtime/config/`.

`workerBridge.mjs` still constructs the worker from `./llama_worker/llama.mjs`, and `llama_worker/llama.mjs` still resolves the configured model path from the worker file location.

## Moved modules

Parent runtime internals were moved into these folders:

```text
runtime/lifecycle/nativeBoundaryCoordinator.mjs
runtime/lifecycle/nativeOperationPolicy.mjs
runtime/lifecycle/runtimeInitCoordinator.mjs
runtime/lifecycle/runtimeLifecycleState.mjs
runtime/lifecycle/runtimeModelResetCoordinator.mjs
runtime/lifecycle/runtimeSessionResetCoordinator.mjs
runtime/lifecycle/runtimeShutdownCoordinator.mjs
runtime/lifecycle/workerProtocolRouter.mjs
runtime/observability/observer.mjs
runtime/request/request.mjs
runtime/request/runtimeRequestSettlement.mjs
runtime/request/scheduler.mjs
runtime/stream/normalizer.mjs
runtime/stream/streamController.mjs
```

Historical notes before this one may still mention the old flat module paths because they describe earlier branch states.

## Test fixture propagation

Fixture-copy `RUNTIME_FILES` lists were updated to use the nested runtime paths where required. The fixture copy helpers already create destination parent directories recursively, so nested runtime paths remain copyable in temporary smoke-test repos.

## Behavior boundaries preserved

This layout branch preserves:

```text
queue-based concurrency
worker as native/model execution boundary
parent runtime ownership of request lifecycle
parent-side stream shaping
config as primary tuning surface
cancelPrompt fast path
workerBridge generation guard behavior
worker protocol message shape
init/reset/shutdown semantics
model path/model identity non-overrideability
```

## Verification focus

Recommended verification for this branch remains:

```bash
find . -name '*.mjs' -print0 | sort -z | xargs -0 -n1 node --check
grep -R "inference\.mjs" -n --include='*.mjs' .
SKIP_REAL_RUNTIME=1 node ./tests/smokeTestNativeOperationHardStopPolicy.mjs
SKIP_REAL_RUNTIME=1 node ./tests/smokeTestWorkerOperationSerialization.mjs
SKIP_REAL_RUNTIME=1 node ./tests/smokeTestInitThenResetWithoutPriorPrompt.mjs
SKIP_REAL_RUNTIME=1 node ./tests/smokeTestContextCreationRetry.mjs
SKIP_REAL_RUNTIME=1 node ./tests/smokeTestContextCreationCancelBoundary.mjs
SKIP_REAL_RUNTIME=1 node ./tests/smokeTestWorkerNativeCancellationBoundary.mjs
SKIP_REAL_RUNTIME=1 node ./tests/smokeTestDrainShutdown.mjs
SKIP_RUNTIME=1 node ./tests/smokeTestHardwareAwareInitRetry.mjs
```

If this branch is uploaded and considered for merge readiness, Michael-side real-runtime checks should still be run because fixture paths and runtime imports changed.
